      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Neutrophils accumulate in the ischemic myocardium and exacerbate postischemic cardiac dysfunction and injury. The formation of lipoxygenase metabolites of AA, derived either directly from the neutrophils or by interactions with other blood elements or cells, may promote neutrophil-mediated injury. Recognition of the roles played by neutrophils and AA metabolites in reperfusion injury may lead to the development of new therapies that can be used in conjunction with thrombolytic drugs to reduce the complications associated with restoring blood flow to the ischemic heart."},
